msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:154
msgid "New secret created. All solved blocks are invalid now, visitors mine once more."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:168
msgid "Lockdown settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:170
msgid "PoWned lockdown is in log-only mode: nothing is blocked, the paths it would challenge are being counted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:177
msgid "PoWned lockdown is active: the server is under heavy load, every page view needs a solved block. It switches off by itself 15 minutes after the load drops."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: time left, e.g. "2 hours"
#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:180
#, php-format
msgid "PoWned lockdown is active: every page view needs a solved block. Search engines, link previews and price comparison sites only see the challenge page. Switches off by itself in %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:182
msgid "PoWned lockdown is active without a time limit: every page view needs a solved block. Search engines, link previews and price comparison sites only see the challenge page. Remember to switch it off."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: directory
#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:201
#, php-format
msgid "Early check is on, but the loader could not be written to %s. The check still runs, just a little later during loading."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:204
msgid "A page cache is active (WP_CACHE). Cached pages are served before PoWned runs. Make sure your cache plugin never caches the protected URLs (for example URLs with query strings; LiteSpeed caches them by default)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:209
msgid "PHP sees a private or reserved visitor address, which usually means a reverse proxy is in front. All visitors then share one network, and one solved block unlocks the site for everyone. Pass the real client address with the powned_client_ip filter (see the README), or set \"Bound to\" to \"Not bound\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:214
msgid "Forwarded address headers (X-Forwarded-For, CF-Connecting-IP) differ from the visitor address: a reverse proxy or CDN is in front. All visitors then share the proxy's network. PoWned never trusts those headers on its own, they are easy to fake. Pass the real client address with the powned_client_ip filter (see the README), or set \"Bound to\" to \"Not bound\"."
msgstr ""

