#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:412
msgid "Query parameters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:414
msgid "One per line, * as wildcard. A URL with any of these parameters is protected. The defaults cover WooCommerce filters (attributes, price, rating, stock, sale)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:415
msgid "Paths"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:417
msgid "Protect whole pages by path, one per line, * as wildcard (e.g. /shop/* for everything below /shop/). Leave empty to protect by parameters only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:418
msgid "Never protect"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:420
msgid "Paths that are always let through, one per line. The admin area and login are always excluded."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:421
msgid "Protected actions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:423
msgid "Checkout and express payment buttons"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:424
msgid "Coupon codes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:425
msgid "Login forms (wp-login.php and the WooCommerce account page)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:426
msgid "Contact Form 7 and comments"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:428
msgid "These actions are only accepted with a solved block. On the pages where they happen (cart, checkout, product pages, login, forms) the browser mines in the background, and forms wait the moment it takes. No challenge page, no puzzle. Visitors without JavaScript cannot use protected actions. Logged-in users always pass. Payment webhooks and gateway callbacks are never checked, whatever the payment provider."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:429
msgid "Checkout also shows the challenge page when someone opens the checkout without a block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:430
msgid "Stealth mode"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:431
msgid "Challenge page shows only a small spinner instead of the block"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:432
msgid "The spinner appears after 0.6 seconds, so quick solves look like a normal page load."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:433
msgid "Early check"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:434
msgid "Run the check before other plugins load (adds a small file to mu-plugins)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:435
msgid "Recommended: a crawler request then costs almost no server time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:438
msgid "Full lockdown"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:439
msgid "For emergencies only. While the lockdown is active, every page view needs a solved block. Before you switch it on:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:441
msgid "Search engines only see the challenge page. It is sent as \"503, try again later\", so a few hours do no harm, but days can cost rankings or pages in the index. Keep \"Let search engines through\" on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:442
msgid "Link previews in messengers and social networks, price comparison sites, product feeds (Google Merchant and similar) and uptime monitors cannot read your pages. Feeds may report errors and ads may be paused."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:443
msgid "Visitors without JavaScript or with cookies blocked cannot open the site at all. On old phones, a raised difficulty can take several seconds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:444
msgid "Every new visitor waits a moment on the first page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:445
msgid "Pages your cache serves before WordPress loads are not checked (cheap anyway). The lockdown slows down bots that drive a real browser, it does not stop them, and it does not help against network-level DDoS."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-powned-settings.php:446
msgid "Not affected: payment webhooks and callbacks of any provider, the REST API, Ajax, feeds, sitemaps, robots.txt, the thank-you page, logged-in users. Try \"Log only\" first to see which pages would be challenged."
msgstr ""

